rivatives. In February, ICE made a surprising $30-billion-plus takeover offer for online retailer eBay, but quickly abandoned the deal after investors expressed their skepticism by bidding down the stocks of both companies. Still, ICE\u2019s share price has nearly doubled over the past five years.</p>"}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2020, "rank": 459, "itemDescription": "Also known as ICE, this Atlanta-based company owns exchanges for financial and commodity markets, including the New York Stock Exchange. ICE also offers trading and clearing services in futures and OTC markets and provides data-analytics services."}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2019, "rank": 469, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2018, "rank": 477, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "future", "title": "The Future 50", "year": 2017, "rank": 18, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2017, "rank": 437, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "100-fastest-growing-companies", "title": "100 Fastest-Growing Companies", "year": 2017, "rank": 34, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2016, "rank": 529, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "100-fastest-growing-companies", "title": "100 Fastest-Growing Companies", "year": 2016, "rank": 62, "itemDescription": ""}, {"slug": "fortune500", "title": "Fortune 500", "year": 2015, "rank": 565, "itemDescription": ""}]}